# Metro imports (Expo / Windows)

Metro can fail with `Unable to resolve "./Foo"` for a sibling file that exists on disk—especially right after creating several new modules in one change. Prefer path-alias imports.

## Do

```tsx
// Sibling / colocated under src/
import { LedgerDayCell } from '@/src/screens/dev/ledger-month/components/LedgerDayCell';
import { loadLedgerMonth } from '@/src/screens/dev/ledger-month/mock/loadLedgerMonth';

// Tiny one-off used only here → keep in the same file (no extra module)
function FilterChip({ label, active, onPress }: Props) { /* … */ }
```

## Do not

```tsx
// Fragile on Windows Metro after adding new files in the same turn
import { FilterChip } from './FilterChip';
import { FilterChip } from './FilterChip.tsx'; // also avoid; Metro does not want extensions
```

## Also

- Use the `@/` alias (project root) for anything under `src/`, including same-folder components.
- Relative `../` for types next door is OK if stable; when in doubt, use `@/src/…`.
- After adding many new files, if resolve fails: switch the import to `@/src/…` or inline a single-use helper—do not assume the file is missing.
